course: dictionary
lesson: 12006
title: Cheeky words and bold behaviour
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cheekiness is a noun. It is a name for a behaviour, the way someone acts. Sometimes it means playful rudeness that shows a lack of respect, and sometimes it means boldness, having the nerve to ask for something.
explain: Use the context to choose the right meaning. «The little boy's cheekiness made the whole class giggle.» The giggling tells you the behaviour was playful and funny, not cruel. «Her cheekiness got her into trouble when she answered back to the teacher.» Here the answering back shows the rudeness, and the trouble shows it was not allowed.
explain: Cheekiness can be a telling-off word or a fond one. Listen to the feeling in the sentence. «What cheekiness!» can be cross, or it can be a smile. A similar word is cheek: «What a cheek, asking for a second pudding!» Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and asking whether it still makes sense.
fact: Cheekiness is a noun, so it names the behaviour itself.
fact: «Cheekiness» can mean playful rudeness that shows a lack of respect.
fact: «Cheekiness» can also mean boldness: the nerve to ask for or do something.
fact: Cheekiness can be a telling-off word or a fond one; the context shows which.
fact: «Cheek» is a similar word, as in «What a cheek!»
exercise: «Her cheekiness made the whole class giggle, but she did not mean any harm.» What does cheekiness mean here? | Running very fast | *Playful rudeness that shows a lack of respect | Being very quiet and shy | Kindness to animals
exercise: «What a cheek, asking for a second pudding!» Which word is most similar to cheek? | *Cheekiness | Sleepiness | Calmness | Weather
exercise: What kind of word is cheekiness? | A word for a colour | A question word | *A noun, a name for a behaviour | A verb, an action word
test: Why did the teacher not really mind the cheekiness? «The boy grinned and said, "Can I have a sticker too?" and the teacher laughed.» | It was a mistake in maths | It was dangerous | *It was playful and funny | It was cruel
test: Which meaning fits cheekiness as boldness? | Losing a race | Being ill in bed | Being afraid of the dark | *Having the nerve to ask for something
exam: Maya asked the head teacher if she could have the day off, and her teacher said, «What cheekiness!» What does the teacher mean? | Maya was sleeping in class | Maya was feeling ill | *Maya was bold and asked for something unusual | Maya was very tall for her age
